)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8bf93e45b3057b6928f89603c629f7b7688b8ad9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n If <img src=\"/media/6f6c0f8aa94c7034120e198bb26a2dd9f97d8468.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then the value of <img src=\"/media/79f1f7d2966821bdb720b8938962510db5d0ef50.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p>\n 3 (3.00 - 3.00)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c2c838b7f3b79c60e8c55e52b0805a6d4e37bd9a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The direct form of an FIR filter is shown below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/783b1bdb8657231a6afc2cb3b8b44ce7b9ccd497.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The input given is <img src=\"/media/d45c1306d1808cfa1b0706ab2cc154d905476a7a.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and the output is <em>y</em>[<em>n</em>]. Then the value of y[2] will be ________ .<br />\n (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.24","high":"0.26"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.25 (0.24 - 0.26)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f2bafab54976115342a662c3d7d5a91b73b7870b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the system defined by the difference equation <img src=\"/media/a79eae70af25f6a4509a9c62a53babbc3fd8ae02.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> where <em>a</em> and <em>b</em> are real and <img src=\"/media/e2330ac6bad9d81bc3e51dc12523813f1abb9ccc.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Then the relation between a and b that must exist if the frequency response is to have a constant magnitude for all ‘ω’ i.e, <img src=\"/media/1f26fa844687177d145db56d09d05cc93aa9e042.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /